// AcquireSeedOnceInput Finite one-shot admission body with two mutually exclusive config input sources. input_source=current_input carries the complete unsaved draft: no candidate row is required, the server resolves the draft against the current globals and the global parser-policy default inside the admission transaction and freezes the captured input as the execution identity. input_source=saved_revision carries candidate_id plus revision and admits against that exact immutable revision. A legacy body with candidate_id+revision and no input_source is accepted with the unchanged saved-revision parsing, selection semantics and replay identity. Carrying a draft together with candidate_id/revision, or a discriminator naming a different source than the supplied fields, is a 400 INPUT_SOURCE_INVALID with zero writes. A one-shot names its seed directly: it is never bound by the configuration's group selection, and the seed's exact persisted snapshot is what proves it exists. A human discovery-provider draft (anibt or mikan) admits a seed of its own catalog entry from any of that entry's groups. A human custom draft admits only a custom seed: under input_source=saved_revision the server derives the custom-source and custom-group identities from the revision's own frozen locator and group under the exact candidate revision identity, and a seed carrying any other entry/group is a 422 SEED_PREVIEW_STALE with zero writes; under input_source=current_input the draft is the one-shot's own unsaved configuration (never written back to the preset), so no saved scope applies and the seed's persisted custom snapshot is the binding. A human origin=oneshot draft is 422 ONE_SHOT_CALLER_INVALID except for one keyword search seed: its refs are the derived search-scope/search-query pair, and it requires a current_input admission plus the exact fresh search snapshot. That narrow exception does not admit a feed or custom seed, a saved revision, or a seed without the search snapshot identity. The agent authorization boundary is unchanged: an agent request still needs a complete origin=oneshot draft and an explicit authorization snapshot, and a human request never gains agent reach.
type AcquireSeedOnceInput struct {
	CandidateId *ID `json:"candidate_id,omitempty"`

	// Draft The complete unsaved draft captured by a current_input admission. Required for input_source=current_input and forbidden otherwise.
	Draft *AnimeDraft `json:"draft,omitempty"`

	// EpisodeOffset The one episode offset of this one-shot. It is written to the one-shot's placeholder RSS link and frozen into the input snapshot and the idempotency request identity; it is never read from an existing subscription, link or the submitted draft. Omitted means 0. Out of range is a 422 OFFSET_OUT_OF_RANGE with zero writes.
	EpisodeOffset *int `json:"episode_offset,omitempty"`

	// InputSource Config input source discriminator. Omitted means the legacy saved-revision body (candidate_id + revision).
	InputSource *AcquireSeedOnceInputInputSource `json:"input_source,omitempty"`
	Revision    *int64                           `json:"revision,omitempty"`

	// SelectedSeed The seed a one-shot admits, in one of two forms. Locator form (the frontend and HTTP path): locator, title and published_at are required, the snapshot identity (snapshot_id, snapshot_version, snapshot_content_hash, stable_seed_key) binds the seed to the persisted feed snapshot it was copied from, and at least one strong content identity (info_hash or expected_payload_digest) is mandatory. Reference form (agents; no download URL ever leaves the server): locator is omitted and snapshot_id, snapshot_version, snapshot_content_hash and stable_seed_key name one seed of one persisted snapshot of the provider/provider_entry_ref/provider_group_ref feed. The server reads that exact snapshot and resolves the seed into the locator form before anything is hashed or frozen, so the frozen input snapshot, the replay identity and every later stage are exactly those of the locator form for the same seed. A missing, superseded, stale or mismatching snapshot, or a stable_seed_key that is not in it, is a 422 SEED_PREVIEW_STALE with zero writes (refresh the snapshot and choose again). Seed facts (title, published_at, size_bytes, info_hash, expected_payload_digest) are optional in the reference form; each supplied fact must equal the snapshot's value or the request is a 422 SEED_PREVIEW_STALE. A reference without the complete snapshot identity is a 422 SEED_INVALID. Replaying the same Idempotency-Key with the same reference returns the original handle even after the snapshot was superseded. A custom seed (provider=custom) is the locator-form seed of one frozen custom/oneshot draft source's own feed snapshot: provider_entry_ref is that snapshot's frozen custom-source identity, provider_group_ref its frozen custom-group identity, and the seed identity inside it is stable_seed_key plus a strong content identity (info_hash or expected_payload_digest). The custom source identity is derived by the server from the draft's own frozen locator and group, so a seed whose entry/group does not belong to the submitted draft is a 422 SEED_PREVIEW_STALE with zero writes.
	SelectedSeed SelectedSeedInput `json:"selected_seed"`
}

