// DownloadCompletionRules The Global download_completion setting (schema download-completion-v2), edited only in the settings page; there is no per-anime override and no draft field. It decides what happens to the qBittorrent task after an acquisition succeeded and all its file operations are terminal. seed keeps the task running (the default). pause stops it, keeping task and files. remove deletes the task and keeps its files. remove_with_data asks qBittorrent to delete the task together with the task's own files; unclassified files, kinds the product does not process and files in sub-folders go with it. remove_with_data refuses when it cannot prove no media-library file lies inside the task's content. seed may carry seed_limits, which are written to qBittorrent once at completion; qBittorrent applies them, the product runs no timer. The value is resolved and frozen when the release is accepted; a later edit never changes an accepted acquisition. Only a succeeded acquisition acts; a failed one keeps its task so a retry can adopt it again.
